  <section class="section"><div class="container detail-grid"><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">On-site oversight</span><h3 style="margin-top:16px">A disciplined eye on progress, quality and cost.</h3><p>Clear reporting and coordinated decisions help keep the project moving in the right direction.</p><a class="btn" href="/#contact">Talk about your site <span>↗</span></a></aside><div class="detail-copy"><p class="lead">Construction is where design intent meets the realities of time, budget, trades and materials. Active coordination helps protect the original brief.</p><h2>Technical management</h2><ul><li>Coordination of contractors, suppliers and appointed consultants.</li><li>Site progress reviews and milestone tracking.</li><li>Monitoring of workmanship against agreed specifications and project requirements.</li><li>Recording of issues, decisions, variations and actions.</li><li>Coordination of inspections, samples and key handover items.</li></ul><h2>Economic management</h2><ul><li>Review of progress claims and cost reporting against the agreed budget.</li><li>Tracking of variations and potential additional costs.</li><li>Comparison of contractor proposals and clarification of exclusions.</li><li>Forward-looking reporting on commitments, risks and forecast costs.</li></ul><h2>Quality without unnecessary complexity</h2><p>Our approach is structured and proportionate to the scale of the project. The client receives a clearer picture of what has been completed, what needs attention and which decisions are needed next. Formal statutory site supervision, safety coordination and certifications are assigned to professionals holding the required appointments and qualifications.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Built around your interests</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Our coordination is designed to support informed decisions, transparent communication and a consistent focus on agreed quality standards.</p></div></div></div></section>
